OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,382,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38102
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1785683880
OL,3,CDad climbs Snowdon after being told
OL,4,Che'll never walk again
OL,6,FBut thanks to specialists at Stoke
OL,7,FMandeville's spinal unit, and his
OL,8,Fsheer determination, he's made it to
OL,9,Fthe top of the mountain.
OL,11,F"My brain has blocked out the
OL,12,Faccident, " he said, "I can't remember
OL,13,Fany of it.
OL,15,F"I just remember waking up in hospital
OL,16,Fand I couldn't feel my legs.
OL,18,F"I was terribly, terribly upset and
OL,19,Fsad thinking that I couldn't be a good
OL,20,Fdad to my daughter. It killed me,
OL,21,Fabsolutely."
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G2/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,382,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38103
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1785683880
OL,3,CDad climbs Snowdon after being told
OL,4,Che'll never walk again
OL,6,FBut despite his surgeon's dire
OL,7,Fprediction, Sam put every effort into
OL,8,Fproving him wrong, and gradually he
OL,9,Fstarted to get movement back into his
OL,10,Flower limbs.
OL,12,FAfter two months at the John Radcliffe
OL,13,FHospital he was transferred to Stoke
OL,14,FMandeville's spinal unit, and began
OL,15,Fthe process of learning to walk again.
OL,17,F"I started off crawling, then I moved
OL,18,Fto standing with a frame, it's like a
OL,19,Fbaby walker but for adults.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G3/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,382,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38104
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1785683880
OL,3,CDad climbs Snowdon after being told
OL,4,Che'll never walk again
OL,6,F"It basically straps you up and you're
OL,7,Fwalking around in a baby walker trying
OL,8,Fto get your feet to work."
OL,10,FJust three weeks after leaving Stoke
OL,11,FMandeville he was able to walk down
OL,12,Fthe aisle at his own wedding.
OL,14,F"I remember when I arrived at Stoke I
OL,15,Fsaid 'I'm not leaving here until I'm
OL,16,Fon my feet'. I have to stay here until
OL,17,FI'm on my feet, I have to because I
OL,18,Fhave to be a dad, I have to be a
OL,19,Fhusband, it has to happen.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G4/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext PageBS-SE Eng NewsCThis DayFReg TV
FL,382,380,120,260,000,100
PN,38105
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F381A1785683880
OL,3,CDad climbs Snowdon after being told
OL,4,Che'll never walk again
OL,6,F"So walking down the aisle at the
OL,7,Fwedding for me, it was emotional yeah,
OL,8,Fbut for me I was like 'I knew it would
OL,9,Fhappen'."
OL,11,FThat attitude helped him climb Mount
OL,12,FSnowdon - just 16 months after the
OL,13,Faccident.
OL,15,FHe dedicted the nine-hour challenge to
OL,16,Fother patients he met on the spinal
OL,17,Funit.
OL,1,W~s1x0~s1~s hw1~k4~c1 hw}h7}j7}   G5/6
OL,2,W,.!" ,.!+, "-$/*%+.!+,*%/*%/*-'T(,,,,,,
